# Wrong-geometry warning (selftest: must FAIL): broken-unknown-module calls a
# module that does not exist. OpenSCAD only WARNs, skips the call and renders
# EMPTY — exactly what the `empty` check below asks for, over a mesh that is
# not the design's. The gate reads the render log and fails on the WARNING
# instead of measuring the nothing it left behind.
stops stop 0
empty broken-unknown-module
empty-control broken-solid
